# Internationalization Error Handling Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines define standardized approaches for handling errors related to internationalization in the Flutter Chat Application. They apply to all error cases including missing translations, formatting errors, and locale-specific issues. Following these rules ensures a consistent user experience across different languages and regions.

## Best Practices
- Always provide fallback translations for critical UI elements
- Handle missing translations gracefully with fallback to default language
- Log missing translations but don't crash the application
- Validate translation parameters at runtime where feasible
- Use try-catch blocks around complex ICU message formatting
- Implement graceful degradation for unsupported locales
- Document expected behavior for missing translations

## Handling Missing Translations
- Implement a fallback chain: requested locale → default locale → hardcoded string
- Show the key name only as a last resort in development builds
- In production, never show translation keys to end users
- Consider visual indicators for untranslated strings in debug mode
- Record metrics on missing translations for later analysis
- Example:
  ```dart
  String getTranslatedText(BuildContext context, String key, {Map<String, dynamic>? args}) {
    try {
      // Try to get the translation using the generated code
      final translation = args == null 
          ? getTranslation(context, key) 
          : getTranslationWithArgs(context, key, args);
      return translation;
    } catch (e) {
      // Log the error and provide fallback
      logMissingTranslation(key, e);
      return getFallbackTranslation(key) ?? 'Missing translation';
    }
  }
  ```

## Parameter Validation
- Validate parameter types before formatting messages
- Handle null or invalid parameters with sensible defaults
- Use conditional formatting based on parameter values
- Example:
  ```dart
  String userStatusMessage(BuildContext context, DateTime? lastSeen) {
    if (lastSeen == null) {
      return context.l10n.userStatusUnknown;
    }
    
    final now = DateTime.now();
    final difference = now.difference(lastSeen);
    
    if (difference.inMinutes < 1) {
      return context.l10n.userStatusJustNow;
    } else if (difference.inHours < 1) {
      return context.l10n.userStatusMinutesAgo(difference.inMinutes);
    } else {
      return context.l10n.userStatusWithTime(lastSeen);
    }
  }
  ```

## RTL/LTR Handling
- Use Directionality widgets when mixing text directions
- Test UI layout in both RTL and LTR modes
- Ensure icons and directional elements respect text direction
- Handle bidirectional text correctly with Unicode control characters when needed
- Example:
  ```dart
  Widget buildMessage(BuildContext context, String message, bool isRTL) {
    return Directionality(
      textDirection: isRTL ? TextDirection.rtl : TextDirection.ltr,
      child: Text(
        message,
        textAlign: isRTL ? TextAlign.right : TextAlign.left,
      ),
    );
  }
  ```

## Format-Specific Errors
- Handle date/time format errors with fallback formats
- Provide sensible defaults for number formatting issues
- Implement custom formatters for complex formatting needs
- Document expected behavior for each format type
- Example:
  ```dart
  String formatCurrency(BuildContext context, double? amount, String currencyCode) {
    if (amount == null) {
      return context.l10n.notAvailable;
    }
    
    try {
      return context.l10n.currencyFormat(amount, currencyCode);
    } catch (e) {
      // Fallback to basic formatting
      return '$currencyCode ${amount.toStringAsFixed(2)}';
    }
  }
  ```

## Testing & Validation
- Write unit tests for all error handling code
- Simulate missing translations during testing
- Test with invalid parameters and edge cases
- Verify fallback behavior works as expected
- Test RTL/LTR switching and mixed directional content
- Validate all plural forms are handled correctly
- Create visual regression tests for layout issues

## Monitoring & Analysis
- Track missing translation rate in analytics
- Implement detection for repeated fallback usage
- Create a dashboard for translation coverage and errors
- Set alerts for sudden increases in translation errors
- Monitor performance impact of complex formatting
- Regularly audit logs for internationalization issues

## Documentation for Translators
- Document all special formatting constructs
- Provide context and visual examples for each string
- Highlight variable length content and UI constraints
- Document plural rules specific to each language
- Create guidelines for maintaining consistent terminology
